==English==
{{wikipedia|The Bronx}}

===Etymology===
{{blend|lang=en|Bronck|-'s}}. After immigrant settler {{w|lang=en|Jonas Bronck}} (1600–1643) of [[New Netherlands]] onto the peninsula north of Manhattan Island.
* {{sense|region}} Originally ''{{l|en|Bronck's Land}}'', the land in the region settled by Jonas Bronck.
* {{sense|river}} Originally ''{{l|en|Bronck's River}}'', a river bordering the region settled by Jonas Bronck.

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{ellipsis of|lang=en|The Bronx}}. A [[borough]] of [[New York City]].
# {{ellipsis of|lang=en|Bronx River}}. A [[river]] downstate in [[New York State]].

====Usage notes====
The term is always preceded by the [[definite article]] "the", and thus expressed as ''the Bronx''.

